+---
+id: dl-001-rental-module-toolchain-typescript-build-to-dist-tests-on-dist
+type: decision-log
+title: "Rental module toolchain: TypeScript build to dist, tests on dist"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Context
+
+The repository is TypeScript with no runtime dependency, and `tsconfig.json` already compiles `src`
+to `dist` with NodeNext module resolution. The repository had no compiler installed and no build
+step, and `npm test` ran `node --test` on raw files. Node 22 runs `.ts` files only through type
+stripping, which requires `.ts` import specifiers and cannot be type-checked by the existing
+`tsconfig.json`.
+
+# Decision
+
+- `typescript` is a development dependency, pinned to the 5.9 line.
+- `npm run build` runs `tsc`, which compiles `src` to `dist`.
+- `npm test` builds first, then runs `node --test` on the compiled `dist` tests.
+- Tests are written in `src` as `*.test.ts` and compile to `dist`, so the NodeNext `.js` import
+  specifiers stay as they are.
+
+# Consequences
+
+- A clean checkout needs `npm install` before `npm test`. The `dist` and `node_modules` directories
+  are already ignored by git.
+- No runtime dependency is added. The only new dependency is the compiler.
