--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-003-item-ids-are-unique-and-quotes-do-not-check-availability.md
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+---
+id: dl-003-item-ids-are-unique-and-quotes-do-not-check-availability
+type: decision-log
+title: "Item ids are unique and quotes do not check availability"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Context
+
+The brief says `quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item or a disallowed period, and that `book`
+also throws when the item is not free. It does not say what `quote` does when the item is busy, nor
+what `addEquipment` does when an id is added twice.
+
+# Decision
+
+- `addEquipment` rejects an id that is already in use. Equipment is never silently replaced, so a
+  booking cannot end up attached to a different item than the one it was made against.
+- `quote` does not check availability. A quote states the price of a period, and a busy item still
+  has a price. Only `book` checks for overlap.
+- Two bookings of the same item overlap when their periods share at least one day. The check uses
+  half-open intervals, so a booking that ends at midnight does not overlap one that starts then.
+
+# Consequences
+
+- A client that wants to show whether an item is free must call `book` or add a separate
+  availability query. That query is not part of this module yet.
+- Rejecting duplicate ids forces a caller to choose unique ids. That is stricter than the brief, but
+  it prevents silent data loss.
